  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4602.03 Acid Rain Program",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-03-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4602.03 “Acid Rain Program” means a multi-state sulfur dioxide and nitrogen oxides air pollution control and emission reduction program established by the Administrator of the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) under title IV of the CAA and 40 CFR Parts 72 through 78.\n\nSource. #9283, INTERIM, eff 10-1-08, EXPIRED: 3-30-09\n\nNew. #9444, eff 4-3-09; ss by #10468, eff 1-1-14 (from Env-A 4602.04); ss by #12967, eff 1-1-20",
